nswer/value "images/37/37597a2cecae00cca3eacec7265913070de9343be6afb9108644d6c8d0c1d93b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487774} {:answer/id #uuid "830b2441-7bb1-5d59-9a62-feb78c7e6ef1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/61/61121fd2f10227f127984cfa0ca6954fb97d0e70bf677244b83e2f0f536ab551.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487816} {:answer/id #uuid "cecc3d11-f1e4-50e7-9dee-b9454f776c20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/2b/2bf599bb1c6bb72971ce9aa76caad4499396d5ebd50d694b3deec2e63b5cc1df.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487964}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487774} :answer-field/id #uuid "4384a499-6a6b-50cc-85bd-25bcfa32de9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "353c7243-8109-54a9-8124-e25ba2a61d98" :question/math-academy-id "q-98680" :question/problem "Which of the following is *not* a simply connected region?" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/46/46305c070e2563b4dacf8b31c88c46b860f003b20ffdff608a5485c09a91bd11.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/a0/a0459ddbabbd810e43db084f5dd174437340914b53ed227f6ef7ce2e3a0fc383.png)\n\nAmong the given options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following:  \n\n![](images/37/37597a2cecae00cca3eacec7265913070de9343be6afb9108644d6c8d0c1d93b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488220 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b8a5532-5c40-544b-a662-5333cce8382a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c0/c0add6c5feca5255760a8bcbd84f68cb425263c857379cb4f1415e8b4e199753.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487715} {:answer/id #uuid "5a9928f1-71c1-540b-85e1-01ff04dab2b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/54/54a73ee1a01be78d548a7e609a05538754e488f57b0a755e7e5f6e2264e14a74.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487750} {:answer/id #uuid "7d6e9b6f-a94b-5109-8c6a-97935704bcdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/65/65e1c034f836802bb8127e754f0e1cb303144468b041d51da2ee1b8a89de1132.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487809} {:answer/id #uuid "9f7781f5-0705-541a-a940-98edef386fd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/94/94e4f7d31dddfd2b960b027848328d1223899ae3172ec2192bc3bd3fc3c0411d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487864} {:answer/id #uuid "fdfd2f97-0aa0-539a-be6f-7097c1940aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/5f/5fce5e6fb02581d530afa04ae596290eebeb84265131b397a11621160170f20b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488045}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487809} :answer-field/id #uuid "1313a534-7913-5042-9bc0-6c44d0135939" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6a1d02fe-8171-5afa-b624-bbcbed75b5b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-98687" :question/problem "Which of the following is *not* a simply connected region?" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/46/46305c070e2563b4dacf8b31c88c46b860f003b20ffdff608a5485c09a91bd11.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/a0/a0459ddbabbd810e43db084f5dd174437340914b53ed227f6ef7ce2e3a0fc383.png)\n\nAmong the given options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following: \n\n![](images/65/65e1c034f836802bb8127e754f0e1cb303144468b041d51da2ee1b8a89de1132.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488225 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19c71b83-4367-5691-97de-b0703bcb7dd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487619} {:answer/id #uuid "45122bac-b3b8-5e27-afee-d630a49ce537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487702} {:answer/id #uuid "ce3274e2-524f-5cf1-9465-3aafe1e0f1a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487963} {:answer/id #uuid "f527e70a-5ed7-53da-91f5-358e6a505020" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488026} {:answer/id #uuid "f7489938-f03a-5f2b-b530-6e9e1bed624b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488032}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487702} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd56075-39b7-59a8-b93d-bcfc68b83760" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7361f82f-c91c-52b9-80ec-852a74fe03bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-124773" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y+2x\\ge 1\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y-2x\\ne 1\\}$" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y\\ge -2x+1.$ So,   it's a plane region without holes,\n\n- Region II is simply connected.  It's a plane region (a circle) without holes.\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the straight line $y=2x+1.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint half-planes and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}]}
